 prompt 'labels that context <untrusted_ticket_context> and names show_ticket authoritative (completion_verifier.md:26-28)' is refuted by the named file: lines 26-28 of src/rebar/llm/reviewers/completion_verifier.md only grant 'read-only access ... and a read-only show_ticket tool to read this ticket and any related ticket' — they neither declare show_ticket authoritative over the fenced context nor apply the <untrusted_ticket_context> label (that tag originates in workflow/gate_ops.py:229; the prompt's untrusted-input framing begins at line 30).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd3d90e590e08c163","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Root cause 1b ('the model correctly preferred the stale snapshot')","norm_id":"n2c1000d938682be9","priority":0.595,"reason":"veto:cited-reference-inaccurate","scenarios":["A reviewer relies on the stated causal mechanism (prompt precedence) to accept Step 1b's premise that the two gate halves disagree because the model is instructed to prefer show_ticket."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Re-cite the correct source: the <untrusted_ticket_context> fence is emitted at workflow/gate_ops.py:229 and the prompt's untrusted-input framing (lines 30-37) tells the model to treat fenced context as untrusted data — that (not a 'show_ticket is authoritative' statement at 26-28) is the mechanism by which the model prefers its own show_ticket read. Restate 1b in those terms.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"no","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"}